## React Native Review

When asked to review React Native code:

- Flag JS thread blocking: synchronous heavy computation (crypto, parsing, large sorts) on the JS thread without a worker or native offload.
- Flag bridge calls in tight loops or rapid event handlers not batched.
- Flag ScrollView for lists of more than 20 items — use FlatList or SectionList instead.
- Flag missing useCallback/useMemo on event handlers passed to native components.
- Flag memory leaks: event listeners, DeviceEventEmitter subscriptions, timers, or store subscriptions not cleaned up in useEffect return or componentWillUnmount.
- Flag OTA update (CodePush) missing staged rollout or rollback config.
- Flag business logic tangled with inline Platform.OS checks — isolate to platform-specific files.
- Flag deep link params used directly in navigation or API calls without sanitisation.
- Flag unpredictable navigation back-stack patterns.
- Order findings P0 (JS blocking on main path, unsanitised deep link params, memory leak on critical screen) through P3 (minor memoization gap) with file:line and a one-line fix each.
